WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
[Soft instrumental music]
What if your next onboarding guide

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.520
became something people could actually
practise?

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.040
Turn an idea into a hands-on GitHub
exercise

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.160
with GitHub Copilot and the
gh-skills-builder plugin.

5
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.960
For educators, maintainers, enterprises,
startups, and internal training,

6
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.800
this workshop puts you in the architect's
seat.

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.560
Copilot helps draft the content and
scaffold the files.

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.680
You shape the learning experience. One
orchestrator agent and five reusable

9
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.000
skills guide the journey. Outline,
bootstrap, review, publish,

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.970
and orchestrate the whole loop. Install
the toolkit from the Awesome Copilot

11
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.840
marketplace. Start with the outcome.
Define what learners will practise,

12
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.760
what success looks like, and how to check
it. Then turn the approved outline

13
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.720
into a runnable, issue-driven GitHub
Skills exercise.

14
00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.840
The example uses Tailspin Toys to teach
three practical Copilot habits.

15
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.880
Clear repository instructions, consistent
quality reports,

16
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.440
and a report-only QA agent. A small
exercise with a concrete purpose,

17
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.640
checks examine what learners wrote, not
just whether a file exists,

18
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.000
review the findings, approve a targeted
fix, and review again.

19
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.480
Useful feedback helps learners understand
what to improve,

20
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.850
people stay in control of the decisions,
prepare the validation evidence and

21
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:31.920
launch checklist, then pause. Release
readiness is not permission to publish,

22
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.680
and this workshop stops before public
release. Watch the live walkthrough,

23
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.280
then replay the copyable prompts at your
own pace. The website brings the slides,

24
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.640
instructions, and resources together.
Repeatable, observable, inclusive, and

25
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:52.440
human-led. Explore the workshop, get the
plugin, and bring your next idea.

26
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.340
Build a learning experience people can put
into practice.

27
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.000
